WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:05.150
National Route 119, Nikkou Kaidou.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:10.540
This mountain road lined with tall cedar 
trees leads to Nikkou Toushou-guu Shrine,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:17.180
a national treasure with 
over 400 years of history.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.750
The road becomes National Route 120 at the 
intersection of the sacred bridge.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:28.250
<b>1,173m
Above
Sea
Level</b>

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.960
<i>The road rises even higher.</i>

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.250
<i>The long winding road that starts at 
one thousand meters above sea level</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.530
<i>will be the turning point in the 
Inter-High's first-day mountain stage,</i>

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.360
<i>Nikkou Irohazaka.</i>

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:38.980
<i>I've been separated.</i>

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.270
<i>Teshima-san told me to stay 
towards the front, too.</i>

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>He told me to stay with the team.</i>

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.370
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:21.550
<i>RIDE.22 The Pressure of Tag #1</i>

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.740
I see them!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.300
They're here.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.280
There are so many of them.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.050
Go!

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.330
You can do it!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.210
Everyone's riding together.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.580
Are they friends?

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.670
Well, actually...

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:35.590
When the road's gently sloping,
it's easier for everyone to ride together.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.970
The wind resistance is—

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.810
Let's just say they're working together.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.230
But there's a hill ahead, right?

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.230
Yeah.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.690
Then they won't be able 
to ride together anymore.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:47.180
What?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.730
The line they're riding in now 
will get longer and longer.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.040
By the end, they'll be separated.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.040
What?

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:53.940
Separated?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.030
Differences in strength 
become apparent on climbs.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.740
Won't they be lonely?

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:03.240
Each team establishes its own 
strategy so that doesn't happen.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.030
Strategy? Then they'll be fine.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.750
But what if they mess up?

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.740
If that happens,
then they'll have to ride alone.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.050
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:19.170
<i>The six of us just met up.</i>

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.990
<i>But I got swallowed by the pack 
and separated from the others.</i>

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.580
<i>I need to get back to the front.</i>

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.220
<i>Teshima-san and the others are at the front...</i>

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.390
<i>Far ahead, where I can't see them.</i>

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.810
<i>I'll go back. I'll go back. I'll go back!</i>

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.220
<i>I'll get back to the others 
before we enter the mountains.</i>

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.530
I told you, we're not letting 
you go to the front.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.450
After all, you're a climber wearing tag #1.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.210
I just want to get back
 to Teshima-san—to my team.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:48.970
Can't you—

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:49.950
What will you do then?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.460
Receive orders from your team and
ride to win the mountain stage, right?

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:56.630
What?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.200
That's what we fear most.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.420
We have climbers on our teams, too.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.470
The first day's mountain stage 
is the Inter-High's medal.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:11.930
Everyone respects the first day because 
we can fight without restraint.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.170
The red number tag is a badge of pride.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.810
Everyone wants it.
Every team is riding for it.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.910
Sorry, but we need you to stay out of it.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.820
I just... I just...

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.320
I just want to do my job.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.180
Stop Sohoku High School's Onoda, 
the bearer of tag #1.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.890
That's my job.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.660
I plan to do my job, too.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.750
For my team.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.750
<i>Sohoku High School's Onoda, tag #1...</i>

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.540
<i>This is Onoda? He's the 
only one I won't let go.</i>

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.760
<i>I can feel their pressure.</i>

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.760
<i>What do I do? What do I do?</i>

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.410
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.890
What did you learn from Makishima-san?

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.270
Carry on their legacy. Teach him.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.810
Show him with your riding.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.940
<i>Show them with my riding.</i>

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.730
<i>That's right. I have to get to the front.</i>

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.400
<i>The front...</i>

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.500
<i>He asked me to take care of 
Sohoku High School for him.</i>

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:09.690
Move, please!

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:11.700
Please!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.550
Get back in line, #1!

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:14.370
No!

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:22.840
<i>The metal part of my pedal clipped his ankle.</i>

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.940
I'm Yamagata Mogami High School 
second-year Inashiro Bunya.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.960
I'm Mogami's assistant in the mountains.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.850
I won't let you go.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.500
I'd sacrifice my legs to keep you here.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.680
I'll block like my life's at stake.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.530
<i>Win the stage, Kawahara-san.</i>

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.710
<i>The climb has started.
We've entered the mountains.</i>

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.420
The incline has increased sharply 
since we passed Nikkou Station.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.020
The real race starts now. Hang in there.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:51.490
Yes, sir.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.740
What is Onoda-kun doing?

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.540
He's supposed to be good at climbs!

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:59.000
He's really not coming. What happened?

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.380
Should I have dropped 
back to bring him to us?

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.880
<i>Onoda!</i>

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.370
<i>Onoda...</i>

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.130
<i>The pressure of tag #1.</i>

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:12.440
<i>We thought we prepared for everything, 
but we never practiced brushing that off.</i>

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:13.810
<i>Come up to us, Onoda.</i>

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.560
<i>Quickly. Otherwise...</i>

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.640
I'm Nagano Chuou High School's climber.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.110
They call me the Guardian of the Alps.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.130
I am Awagashira Yumichika.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.470
Though he temporarily lead the race,

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.480
he sadly ended up third at 
the end of the mountain stage.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.440
I will vindicate the honor 
of Tatebayashi-senpai.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.910
I'm Shizuoka Fujigawa High School's 
climber Daikanji Haruichi.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.650
Mt. Fuji is my home turf.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.500
There's no mountain taller than Mt. Fuji.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:42.760
Look! It's Yamagata Mogami High School 
third-year Kawahara Gunpei!

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:45.800
Rumor has it he's the strongest 
climber at this tournament!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.070
<i>Bunya, I'm counting on your assistance.</i>

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.430
<i>I'll claim the mountain number tag.</i>

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:52.100
They're so fast!

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:53.350
They're making their move already?

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.930
<i>The climbers are taking 
off one after another.</i>

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.410
<i>Hakone hasn't made their move yet,</i>

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.060
<i>but it's only a matter of time.</i>

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:05.730
We'll slow down as much as 
we can and wait for Onoda.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.740
Whatever you do, don't let
Hakone get farther ahead.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:09.780
Yes, sir.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:12.570
We can't wait any longer.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.720
<i>The pack has stretched out 
since we entered the climb.</i>

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:16.830
<i>I don't see him.</i>

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.330
<i>They're scattered.</i>

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.250
Okay, then.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:25.250
Kabu and I will go rescue 
Onoda-kun real quick.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.680
<i>At some point, I ended up in last place.</i>

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.330
<b>Sohoku</b>

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:40.140
<i>I'm at the end of the stretched-out pack.</i>

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:40.140
<b>Onoda</b>

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.980
<i>I need to get back to the 
group quickly. Quickly.</i>

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.020
<i>I have to do something.</i>

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.580
<i>It's probably not that bad yet.</i>

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.990
<i>If the way in front of me is blocked, then...</i>

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.240
<i>I'll go back.</i>

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.450
He stopped!

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.790
He braked hard! Is he having 
trouble with his bike?

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:00.450
No!

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.310
Crap!

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.210
I wasn't expecting him to 
use being in last place!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.530
Catch him!

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.610
We've already started to enter the climb!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.900
He's unbelievably fast going uphill!

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:16.800
<i>I'll catch up like this.</i>

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:18.970
He's fast!

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.060
You can't be serious! 
How can he accelerate like that?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.160
Ride as hard as you can!

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:23.730
Damn it!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.860
Mogami High School's Inashiro jumped ahead!

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.070
If we don't, he'll get away!

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.080
<i>Don't underestimate me, tag #1.</i>

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.450
<i>I'm Kawahara-san's mountain stage assistant.</i>

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.030
<i>An assistant...</i>

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.600
<i>...has an assistant's pride!</i>

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.770
Stop, Sohoku High School's Onoda!

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:44.710
Yamagata Mogami High School's 
Inashiro cut in front of him!

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.520
Sorry.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.010
That was a little rough, but I 
can't let you get to the front.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.090
Yamagata Mogami High School will 
take the mountain number tag.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.220
You're not getting away, Sohoku High School.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:02.730
<i>Sohoku High School's #1
was last year's champion.</i>

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.700
<i>He's stronger than I expected.
He pedals hard.</i>

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:09.110
<i>I can't believe he rode so awkwardly 
in the middle of the pack.</i>

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:17.200
<i>In a few hundred meters, the seven-man 
blockade we had dropped to three.</i>

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.140
<i>They're blocking me from behind.</i>

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.240
<i>I won't be able to use that again.</i>

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.910
<i>Teshima-san...</i>

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.840
<i>I'll stop him. That's my job.</i>

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.670
<i>I'll do it for Kawahara-san.</i>

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.010
The leaders are here!

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:32.570
It's Nagano Chuou and Shizuoka Fujigawa!

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.350
There's one more behind them!

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:35.380
He's so fast!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.260
It's Yamagata Mogami High School 
third-year Kawahara Gunpei!

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.780
Wow, look at him climb!

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.260
He's not even breaking a sweat!

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.220
He's in first!

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:47.270
<i>Bunya, are you working hard?</i>

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.940
<i>I promise I'll take it this year.</i>

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.730
<i>I'll claim the mountain number tag.</i>

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.530
What do you mean we can't go 
back for him, Teshima-san?

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.810
I meant exactly what I said.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:01.740
I won't allow it.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:03.370
Why not?

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.660
Is it because we're in the mountains?

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.560
Because he'll make it 
back at the last minute?

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.320
I'm saying we should rescue him 
because he hasn't come back.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.200
The other teams are getting in his way.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.130
Anyone would keep last 
year's champion in check.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.310
He can't ride at his own pace.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.270
Kabu and I will go back and get him.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.100
Onoda-kun's never experienced 
something like this.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.880
Shouting at the night's 
darkness won't create light.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.560
All you can do is wait for dawn.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.950
What is that, some kind of riddle?

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:31.100
What? A riddle?

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:34.370
We're in the mountains, 
and Onoda-kun's not here.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.600
There's no telling when
Hakone will make their move.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.990
And you want us to wait in silence?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:41.160
I'm telling you not to act recklessly!

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.320
What?

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:46.060
If we changed our formation,
we'd be playing into their hands.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.330
It may look like they're not paying attention,
 but they're keeping a close eye on us.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.980
If our numbers decrease, they'll attack.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:54.960
We'll fall behind.

00:10:55.350 --> 00:11:00.180
If you and Kaburagi go back, leaving three
of us, it'll be three against six.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.210
They're waiting for 
just that kind of situation.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:07.680
Their goal is to force our 
entire team out of the race.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:08.700
What?

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.060
Then we can't rescue him.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:15.390
We're at an overwhelming disadvantage.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:21.330
We have to climb this mountain without our 
ace climber and two exhausted sprinters.

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:24.070
We're about to start up 
the hellish Irohazaka.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:31.540
And this year's Hakone Academy High School 
has Kuroda, Ashikiba, Manami, and Shinkai.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:33.420
They have four climbers.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.200
<i>Four.</i>

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.650
<i>I noticed Shinkai's little brother 
didn't race in the sprint.</i>

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.300
<i>So he's a climber, huh?</i>

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.730
Then will we give up on 
winning the mountain stage?

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.430
Onoda-san's not back yet.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.690
We can't.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.060
If they make their move, we'll have to, as well.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:53.560
Why? We can just let them 
do whatever they want.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.770
If we do that, they'll head 
straight for the finish line.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.090
<i>What? The finish line?</i>

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:03.660
The results of the mountain stage 
affect the finish line after that.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:07.490
We can't let them take 
the mountains so easily.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:08.990
Aoyagi-san...

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.710
<i>Aoyagi-san said two whole sentences.</i>

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.670
What are we going to do, then?

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.320
I have orders for you.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:17.340
Yes, sir.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.420
Imaizumi...

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:18.840
Yes, sir.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:20.850
<i>Looks like is a job for hotshot.</i>

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:25.020
You and Naruko take turns pulling the 
team and prepare for the finish line.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.820
You're our ace.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:30.870
Without you at the finish line, 
we'll lose what should be ours.

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:33.030
Sorry for making you spend your energy,

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:36.330
but take our exhausted sprinters 
to the top of the mountain.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.360
Exhausted sprinter?

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.450
He must be talking about you.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:43.140
Then who's—

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.680
Hakone's making their move!

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:45.910
<i>They're moving!</i>

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:46.900
<i>Hakone Academy High School!</i>

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:47.990
<i>Who will they send?</i>

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.590
It's nearly time.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:50.990
Go win the mountain stage.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:53.410
Go, Manami.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.210
Yes, sir.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.040
The weather's great today.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:03.260
These kinds of days are the 
most fun for climbing hills.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.040
Hey, Manami. Don't be so relaxed.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:08.010
The other climbers are already climbing.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:10.620
Don't worry, Kuroda-san.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.970
I'll go enjoy the hill.

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:17.230
Strangely enough,
he's managed to hone his skills.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.360
<i>Go, Manami.</i>

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.670
<i>Pass the climbers in front of you.</i>

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:24.690
<i>If things go well, 
take the first day's finish line.</i>

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.930
Are you for real?

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.110
Yes, for real.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.450
Without Onoda, we don't have a choice.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.920
Who will Sohoku High School send?

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:34.660
You can't be serious.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.160
You're challenging the mountains?

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.750
Sorry to be rude, but I don't think
 you have a climber's ability or instinct.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:44.700
Yeah, that's why I'll climb with hard work!

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.760
Hakone's making its move!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.460
The first day's mountain race has begun!

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:56.810
It's last year's second place finisher,
second-year Manami Sangaku!

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.480
Sohoku High School's coming, too!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.690
Is it Onoda?

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:05.110
What? It's not Onoda.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.080
I'm kind of disappointed.

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:09.700
I came to see last year's champion race.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.370
Is he holding back?

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:11.950
No, look at that.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.880
Onoda's not with Sohoku High School?

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:14.790
Is he having problems?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:17.610
Number 5, Teshima Junta.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:19.960
He seemed pretty ordinary.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.940
Abs!

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:24.500
Excuse me.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.380
I mustn't laugh.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.900
I feel sorry for you.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:32.980
Your captain, Teshima-kun, became emotional.

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:36.520
He lost Onoda Sakamichi, the man he meant 
to send, when he was swallowed by the pack.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.630
He felt responsible.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:41.520
He lost his #1 due to his own mistake.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.400
Isn't that right?

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:48.150
But I can't believe he sent himself.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:52.660
Imaizumi-kun, shouldn't you have gone?

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.790
I can tell from watching him so far.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:58.640
He's smart, but he's an unexceptional rider.

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.120
Climb with hard work?

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.670
No, let me be blunt.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:03.880
He doesn't stand a chance...

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:07.830
...against our Manami.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.550
Let me say my piece, too.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:20.810
For the past year, he's been 
working hard every time I saw him.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.480
<i>You think I'm reckless, Izumida?</i>

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.230
<i>Would you stop me, Imaizumi?</i>

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.170
<i>Would you say I don't stand a chance, Naruko?</i>

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.320
<i>I don't blame them. I'm not special.</i>

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.370
<i>On top of that, we're at the Inter-High.</i>

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.750
<i>It's the glorious mountain stage.</i>

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.000
<i>I know this isn't my job.</i>

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:43.710
<i>But I...</i>

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.030
Teshima, you're a climber.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:49.630
<i>I was told to climb.</i>

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:54.590
<i>I was told to put one foot 
in front of the other.</i>

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:57.640
<i>I don't have any special abilities.
I can't leap ahead.</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:02.100
<i>Honestly, once upon a time,
I wanted to be like that.</i>

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.370
<i>But I'll show you, one step at a time...</i>

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:08.550
<i>the ordinary way I ride along the ground.</i>

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.410
Sohoku High School caught up to 
Hakone Academy High School's Manami!

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:13.480
It's #5!

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:14.700
Who's #5?

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:17.370
You're Sakamichi-kun's senpai.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:22.830
Hey. I saw your amazing race to the 
finish last year, Manami Sangaku.

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.750
Let's ride to the peak together, 
since we have the chance.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:29.900
I hate to waste an opportunity...

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.470
But I'm in a bit of a hurry.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:37.550
I was told to win the mountain stage.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:39.870
<i>His acceleration is amazing.</i>

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.730
<i>It's totally different seeing it up close.</i>

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.640
<i>He's fast, but...</i>

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:47.540
I'll catch him!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.280
Let's ride together.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.030
Wow, you caught up.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.530
You're better than I thought.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:59.450
I'm still your elder.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.620
Show some respect and ride slower.

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:06.580
<i>He's not using the wings I've heard about.</i>

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.250
<i>Does that mean he can go even faster?</i>

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:12.810
I still don't see the 
climbers in front of us.

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:15.180
<i>We haven't even entered Irohazaka yet.</i>

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:19.180
<i>Climbing is hard, Makishima-san.</i>

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.850
Ah, found one.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.140
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.390
It's Hakone Academy High School 
and Sohoku High School!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.950
<b>Manami-sama</b>

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.280
He's so cool!

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.510
Hello.

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:48.500
<i>This is Manami Sangaku.</i>

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:51.380
<i>He climbs as though inclines 
are nothing to him.</i>

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.640
<i>We've already passed five of the 
climbers who were riding ahead of us.</i>

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:55.500
Whoa, it's Manami!

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:56.590
Sohoku High School!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:00.180
<i>He's fast. He's horrifyingly fast.</i>

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.470
<i>And he's smiling.</i>

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.810
<i>I can barely keep up.</i>

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.310
Sohoku High School's #5...

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:09.980
He really seemed to be struggling.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.820
<b>Irohazaka Map</b>

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.530
<i>Please, Manami Sangaku.</i>

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:17.570
<i>Don't ride as hard as you can yet.</i>

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.910
They're entering Irohazaka!

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:20.070
<i>We just made it to the entrance of Irohazaka.</i>

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.070
It's Hakone Academy High School's Manami!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.450
There's one Sohoku High School
 rider following him!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.030
Huh? You're amazing.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.160
You're keeping up with me, 
Sakamichi-kun's senpai.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.620
Was your name Kojima-san?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.130
It's Teshima.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:34.730
I'm wearing a Sohoku High School jersey, too.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:36.020
It won't be that easy to—

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.630
Do you like slopes?

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.300
Not particularly.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:41.620
Really?

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.800
Then you don't need to keep up.

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:47.140
You won't make any progress 
doing something you don't like.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.220
<i>Don't say that so casually.</i>

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:53.650
My situation doesn't allow for that.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:57.610
At school, there's a class rep 
who's always getting mad at me.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:59.560
She wears half-moon glasses.

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:04.290
She told me to stop coming late and do 
my homework since I'm a second-year now.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:05.960
She hates bugs,

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:09.370
but she comes to cheer the team on at 
these courses in the middle of nature.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.870
When I asked if she likes 
road races, she said...

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:13.990
Not really.

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:17.960
I don't particularly like bicycles.

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.920
Can you believe it?

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.220
But she's coming again this year.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:25.220
Well, it's close enough 
that I can take the train.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.560
People are so strange, aren't they?

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.800
Maybe.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:37.050
I'm wondering why I'm chasing after first-rate
 Hakone Academy High School climber

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:39.820
Manami Sangaku with such 
an elevated heart rate.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.990
But I always arrive at the same answer.

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:45.330
Ah, found another one.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:48.620
You idiot!

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.620
I wasn't finished talking!

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:53.140
<i>Is this Manami's full acceleration?</i>

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:55.080
<i>He's fast. The timing's totally different.</i>

00:19:56.090 --> 00:20:01.420
<i>I can feel how much stronger he is, 
but don't give up now, Teshima Junta!</i>

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:03.590
Manami!

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:07.600
The man who inherited tag #3 from 
Hakone Academy High School's Mountain God.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:10.670
You won't pass me.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:12.480
I'm Shizuoka Fujigawa High School's Daikanji.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.100
My home turf is Mt. Fuji.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.810
He's unbelievable. He passed me so easily.

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:19.820
Sohoku High School, too?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.380
What? Number 5?

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:22.570
That's their captain, Teshima.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.510
I thought he was their leader.

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:27.400
Why's he chasing after Hakone by himself?

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:31.880
<i>Huh? Teshima wasn't in the race last year.</i>

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.890
<i>He's making his first 
appearance as a third-year?</i>

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:35.780
<i>And he's chasing after him?</i>

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:39.680
<i>Hakone Academy High School's Manami?</i>

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.340
<i>That's impossible. There's no way.</i>

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:45.510
<i>It's reckless, no matter how you look at it.</i>

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.550
Wow. You're amazing, Teshima-san.

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:54.310
You kept up with that.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:58.040
But are you sure you 
should be riding so fast?

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.380
Irohazaka has a long ways to go.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:02.320
And there are still riders in front of us.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:15.860
What? In front of me?

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.290
Don't worry... about me.

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:22.510
I'm Sohoku High School's captain, 
third-year Teshima Junta.

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.550
People laugh at me all the 
time for being ordinary.

00:21:26.190 --> 00:21:30.980
Racing and exhausting you,
Hakone Academy High School's ace climber,

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:36.810
and winning the Inter-High's 
mountain stage is my job!

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:42.440
I'm starting to get interested.

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:51.110
<i>Teshima-san is on the board!</i>

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:26.880
He's so cold when I don't have food.

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.230
Kuroda-san!

00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:29.180
Oh, Manami.

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:31.130
Hey, it's a cat.

00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:34.180
Wow.

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:36.170
Why?

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:36.580
You're so cute.

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:40.020
<i>NEXT RIDE  Sakamichi's Pursuit</i>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:45.020
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:52.000
<b><i>The high cadence
 continues!!</i></b>
